15→\n   116→        :param app: The app configuration to finalize.\n   117→        \"\"\"\n   118→        self.logger.info(\"Finalizing application configuration...\", prefix=app.app_name)\n   119→        freedesktop_info = self.platform_freedesktop_info(app)\n   120→\n   121→        # Process the FreeDesktop content to give the vendor, codename and vendor base.\n   122→        (\n   123→            app.target_vendor,\n   124→            app.target_codename,\n   125→            app.target_vendor_base,\n   126→        ) = self.vendor_details(freedesktop_info)\n   127→\n   128→        self.logger.info(\n   129→            f\"Targeting {app.target_vendor}:{app.target_codename} (Vendor base {app.target_vendor_base})\"\n   130→        )\n   131→\n   132→        if not self.use_docker:\n   133→            app.target_image = f\"{app.target_vendor}:{app.target_codename}\"\n   134→        else:\n   135→            # If we're building for Arch, and Docker does user mapping, we can't build,\n   136→            # because Arch won't let makepkg run as root. Docker on macOS *does* map the\n   137→            # user, but introducing a step-down user doesn't alter behavior, so we can\n   138→            # allow it.\n   139→            if (\n   140→                app.target_vendor_base == ARCH\n   141→                and self.tools.docker.is_user_mapped\n   142→                and self.tools.host_os != \"Darwin\"\n   143→            ):\n   144→                raise BriefcaseCommandError(\n   145→                    \"\"\"\\\n   146→Briefcase cannot use this Docker installation to target Arch Linux since the\n   147→tools to build packages for Arch cannot be run as root.\n   148→\n   149→The Docker available to Briefcase requires the use of the root user in\n   150→containers to maintain accurate file permissions of the build artefacts.\n   151→\n   152→This most likely means you're using Docker Desktop or rootless Docker.\n   153→\n   154→Install Docker Engine and try again or run 